   against a spanning family of perturbations are equal, and — the converse —
   over a proper admitted fibre two distinct tensors always agree, so
   algebraic separation holds *exactly* when the admitted perturbation fibre is
   everything.  Sharpened topologically: a *dense* fibre already separates, and
   over a complete space density is exactly the separation condition —
   the physically attainable form, since a fibre of compactly supported
   perturbations is never everything but can be dense.
51x. `Integration.Variation.CutoffLimit` — finite cutoff to continuum.  The
