   and for infinite summable sector families, and its commutation with the
   cutoff limit; and three negatives — pairing convergence is not tensor
   convergence, a divergent family has no continuum pairing, one sector is not
   the total.
51y. `Integration.Variation.CommonLanguage` — one common metric-variation
